        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): keep bundle LSP tool names provider-safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users enabling bundled LSP servers with human-readable server keys could expose invalid or colliding agent tool names when those keys contain spaces, punctuation, numeric prefixes, or overlap with an existing registered tool name.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe bundle LSP runtime now keeps the original server key for user-facing labels and execution details while deriving a provider-safe model-facing tool prefix for hover, definition, and references tools. The prefix is bounded to the existing 64-character tool-name budget and disambiguated against sibling LSP prefixes plus already registered tool names, matching the bundle MCP naming boundary without changing configuration, provider routing, or LSP protocol behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgents can use bundled LSP hover, definition, and references tools for readable server names such as `Type Script!` or numeric keys, and LSP tools are no longer dropped when the sanitized name would collide with a registered tool.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: at current head `25663d924f98daa0e22337a0b6ecdd6cc650952f`, bundled LSP tool materialization produces provider-safe, unique tool names from unsafe and colliding server keys, avoids a registered tool-name collision, spawns real stdio LSP child processes, and preserves the original server label in tool execution details.\n- Focused regression: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/agent-bundle-lsp-runtime.test.ts` passed with 1 file and 10 tests.\n- Real runtime transcript: `node --import tsx --input-type=module -` ran a repo-local script through `loadEmbeddedAgentLspConfig -> loadEnabledBundleLspConfig -> createBundleLspToolRuntime -> spawn child stdio LSP process -> initialize -> tool materialization -> hover execute` using an enabled file-backed Claude bundle with server keys `Type Script!`, `123`, and `Type-Script-`, plus reserved tool name `lsp_hover_Type-Script-`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"head\": \"25663d924f98daa0e22337a0b6ecdd6cc650952f\",\n  \"childProcessProof\": {\n    \"commandBasename\": \"node.exe\",\n    \"initializedServers\": [\"123\", \"Type Script!\", \"Type-Script-\"],\n    \"hoverServer\": \"Type Script!\",\n    \"distinctChildPids\": 3\n  },\n  \"toolNames\": [\n    \"lsp_definition_Type-Script--2\",\n    \"lsp_definition_Type-Script--3\",\n    \"lsp_definition_lsp-123\",\n    \"lsp_hover_Type-Script--2\",\n    \"lsp_hover_Type-Script--3\",\n    \"lsp_hover_lsp-123\",\n    \"lsp_references_Type-Script--2\",\n    \"lsp_references_Type-Script--3\",\n    \"lsp_references_lsp-123\"\n  ],\n  \"checks\": {\n    \"allProviderSafe\": true,\n    \"allLengthOk\": true,\n    \"unique\": true\n  },\n  \"hoverResult\": {\n    \"toolName\": \"lsp_hover_Type-Script--2\",\n    \"details\": {\n      \"lspServer\": \"Type Script!\",\n      \"lspMethod\": \"hover\"\n    },\n    \"textIncludesOriginalServer\": true\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- Targeted format: `node_modules\\.bin\\oxfmt.CMD --check --threads=1 src\\agents\\agent-bundle-lsp-runtime.ts src\\agents\\agent-bundle-lsp-runtime.test.ts` passed.\n- Committed diff hygiene: `git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD` passed.\n- Review proof: `python .agents\\skills\\autoreview\\scripts\\autoreview --mode commit --commit HEAD` completed with no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Duplicate search: no open self PR with the same root cause; `bundle LSP tool name` and `lsp_hover` open PR searches were empty, and `agent-bundle-lsp-runtime` only found adjacent LSP lifecycle/size PRs rather than a tool-name fix.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I reviewed the bundle LSP runtime path, sibling bundle MCP naming helper, and focused regression coverage.",
